==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OneAuditPerOperation  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_OneAuditPerOperation.als
    rationale: Removing the uniqueness fact lets two distinct AuditEntry atoms share the same ofOp, which is exactly the duplicate/rewrite scenario AppendOnly forbids and which also breaks the 'one' multiplicity in AuditCompleteness.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutable, FR_012_NoDeletionPath, AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AuditOnEveryAttempt
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NoDeletionPath: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AuditOnEveryAttempt: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuthenticationBoundary  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuthenticationBoundary.als
    rationale: Without the boundary fact, Alloy can invent an Operation that has no caller yet does not have outcome=Unauthenticated, i.e., business logic ran without authentication.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGate  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGate.als
    rationale: Removing the care-team gate lets a Permitted LookupPatient exist without any CareTeamMembership row tying the caller to the requested patient — exactly the FR-006 violation.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamMembershipRequired
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamMembershipRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_VisibleResponseMapping  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_VisibleResponseMapping.als
    rationale: Clearing the outcome-to-visible mapping permits an Operation whose outcome is Denied to surface a non-NotFound404 response, which would leak the existence of the patient to a non-care-team clinician.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentDeniedNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentDeniedNotFound: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilegeFact  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilegeFact.als
    rationale: Without the least-privilege fact, Alloy can produce a Permitted operation whose (role, kind) pair is not in PermMatrix.Allowed — e.g., an audit_officer succeeding at LookupPatient, or a doctor succeeding at AuditSearch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_011_AuditOnlyByIG
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_AuditOnlyByIG: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditOnLookup  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditOnLookup.als
    rationale: Clearing the audit-on-lookup fact lets a Permitted LookupPatient operation exist with zero AuditEntry rows pointing at it — exactly the 'record observed without matching audit entry' failure SC-002 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AuditOnEveryAttempt, FR_013_SLAAudit
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AuditOnEveryAttempt: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_SLAAudit: FAIL (expected)

